; Validate labelled, non-skip OCaml code blocks in the files listed
; below with ocaml-mdx. Plain fences and `ocaml skip` are excluded.
; M12-L01/L02 have no mdx stanza; M11 uses a separate compiler.

; Cap the bytecode stack for the mdx runs (the limit is in words).
; The browser worker overflows at ~3-10k frames, so lecture demos
; that rely on Stack_overflow (e.g. the buggy mergesort in
; M09-L05) trip it instantly there; with the native default limit
; the same demo grows the stack for minutes (the GC rescans the
; ever-deeper stack on every minor collection) before overflowing,
; once per QCheck shrink step. 200k words still allows ~25k-deep
; recursion, far beyond anything a legitimate cell needs.
(env
 (_
  (env-vars
   (OCAMLRUNPARAM "l=200000"))))

; Two version-gated mdx stanzas. M01-M10 and M12 validate on the
; default switch (currently 5.4.0); only M11 (OxCaml) validates on
; the 5.2.0+ox switch, where the mode syntax compiles. `enabled_if`
; routes each stanza to exactly one switch: a disabled stanza is
; inert, so stanza 2 below need not have qcheck/ounit2 installed on
; the ox switch, and stanza 1's libraries are not required there.
;
; Run both with: `dune runtest` (default switch) and
; `dune build @lectures/runtest` under `opam exec --switch nptel-ox`.
;
; Stanza 1 (default switch). The libraries are needed by the M09
; cells only (the browser pages load them via m09-extras.js);
; linking them is harmless for M01-M08.
(mdx
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{ocaml_version} 5.2.0+ox))
 (libraries qcheck-core qcheck ounit2 ounit2.advanced)
 (preludes mdx_prelude.ml)
